// TASK 7: Common Misconfigurations and Attacks
$task_contents[7] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <h2>Where Real Integrations Break</h2>
    <p>Every attack against a federation setup exploits a validation check that should have run but did not. None of these require breaking cryptography. They require finding the one field the SP forgot to verify.</p>

    <table class="content-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Flaw</th>
                <th>What It Enables</th>
                <th>Check That Prevents It</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>Signature covers only part of the response</td>
                <td>Attacker modifies unsigned fields undetected</td>
                <td>Signature Scope Validation</td>
            </tr>
