<div class="content-block">
    <p>Federation replaces per-application credentials with a single trust relationship between an Identity Provider and every Service Provider that relies on it. SAML, OAuth, and OpenID Connect each implement a piece of this differently, but they share the same underlying requirement: every claim must be validated in full, not just accepted because it arrived with a signature attached.</p>

    <p>The engineering work is in the details. A signature that does not cover the whole message, a missing audience check, or an expired timestamp all look fine at a glance but each one opens a real path to impersonation.</p>

